+++ b/MIGRATION_SUMMARY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+- `serve_turn` in `serving/harness.py` now drives the turn through `reference_v2.loop.stream_tool_loop`, using the model's `stream()` API instead of `complete()`, and accepts an `on_delta` callback for each streamed text delta while keeping the monitored `RuntimeContext`/`TurnResult` wrapper.
+- I verified streaming by asserting `ScriptedModel.complete_calls == 0`, `stream_calls == 2`, `on_delta` received `["calling ", "done ", "5 "]`, and `serve_turn` produced the expected `user/assistant/tool/assistant` message roles and final text `done 5`.
+- Runtime monitoring: remained active — a monitored turn published `model`, `tool`, `model` events to the configured `MONITOR_EVENTS` file, matching the 2 model-step / 1 tool-call expectation.
